# --- drone snapshot: runtime artifacts never belong in git -------------------
#
# This directory is a point-in-time dump of the drone's `~/aeroshield/` *data*
# dir, pulled over SSH (see `_meta/MANIFEST.md`). Most of it is a legitimate
# archive: the flight record, the offline spool, and the code as it actually ran.
#
# It was committed wholesale, and `~/aeroshield/` is the data dir, which by
# design holds three things that must not be versioned. The repo is public. The
# rules below keep them out from here on.
#
# Note that ignoring a path does not remove it if it is already tracked — the
# committed copies were taken out of the index with `git rm --cached` at the same
# time. They stay on disk and on the drone. Their *history* still contains the
# key, which is why the key was rotated rather than merely untracked.

# The credential itself. `.env.example` documents the shape and stays tracked.
.env*
!.env.example

# The append-only flight record (AGENTS.md). Real survey data — 2234 detections
# from a flown mission. Reproduce it by flying, not by cloning.
logs/

# The offline queue of detections captured while the radio link was down:
# ~2000 frames, ~37 MB. AGENTS.md forbids rsyncing this *to* the aircraft because
# replaying it would look like measured flight data. Same reason it does not
# belong in a public repo.
spool/
